# Release signing. The public half is published deliberately, under
# infra/release-signing/, and must stay tracked. The private half must never be
# in the repository at all -- it is the one secret whose loss lets someone sign
# a release every appliance accepts. release-signing.test.sh enforces this
# independently, because .gitignore does not stop `git add -f`.
*.key
signing-key*
release-signing-private*

# Local working notes. These describe the maintainer's own machine, its paths
# and its internal state, and are written for a single session -- they are not
# documentation and must never be published.
#
# A release cannot leak them today: create-deployment-kit.sh builds the
# deployment archive with `git archive <tag>`, so only tracked files ship. The
# exposure is one `git add -A` away, which is exactly what this prevents.
# Anchored to the repository root so the clinical case-handover feature --
# HandoverButton, use-case-handover, case-handover specs, the handover
# migration -- stays tracked and shipped as normal.
/HANDOVER.md
/*HANDOVER*.md
/*FORCLAUDE*.md
/*BUGFIXES*.md
/LIABILITIES.md
/AUDIT_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md
/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_*.md
